The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to access the second element of the split array, when it should have been using `parts[0]` to get the first element. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because 'hello world'.split(' ')[1] returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error because 'solo'.split(' ')[1] caused an IndexError (the array only has one element at index 0)

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
